  "pass_a_gloss": "God judges the condemned, granting time and not immediately inflicting punishment's end. His example is seen in Leviticus, where prior punishments precede further penalties. He tempers judgment with mercy, desiring repentance rather than total destruction. This pattern applies to the people, with threats followed by promises of non-annihilation. The true punishments are shadowed by those under the law and prophets.",
